---
title: How to check form submissions
sidebar:
  order: 3
---
**To check form submissions, follow these steps:**

1. **Navigate to the Forms Section:**

   - **From the left sidebar of your dashboard, click on the “Forms” section to view all the forms you have created.**

1. **Select Your Form:**

   - **Once in the Forms list, locate the form you want to review submissions for.**
   - **Next to your form name, you’ll see a “Submissions” count (e.g., “6”). Click on this number to access all submissions for that form.**

1. **View the List of Submissions:**

   - **You’ll be taken to a page listing all the submissions for the selected form.**
   - **The list includes details like ID, First Name, Last Name, Email, Preferred Method of Contact, Phone, Product, Budget, Requirements, and IP Address.**

1. **View or Delete a Submission:**

   - **To view more details about a specific submission, click on the eye icon under the Action column.**
   - **If you wish to delete a submission, use the trash icon next to the eye icon.**

1. **View Submission Details:**

   - **Clicking the eye icon opens a detailed view of the submission.**
   - **On the left, you’ll see the Form Data including all the responses the user has submitted.**
   - **On the right, you’ll find the Submission Info such as:**
     - **ID: Unique submission ID.**
     - **User IP: The IP address of the user.**
     - **Country: The country from which the form was submitted.**
     - **Browser: The browser used for the submission.**
     - **Device & OS: Information about the user’s device and operating system.**
     - **Submitted On: The timestamp of when the form was submitted.**

**By following these steps, you can easily access, review, and manage all the submissions for your form.**
